  "gitCommitMessage": "Fix white screen on cold start with no stored session\n\nsrc/app/index.tsx rendered `return null` once AuthContext's isLoading\nflipped false but no token was present yet - the most common case on a\ncold start with no stored session, since restoreSession() resolves almost\ninstantly with nothing to restore. During that window this screen (\"/\")\nwas the only one mounted, waiting for _layout.tsx's own effect (which also\nwaits on fonts and router mount, not just the session) to redirect to\n/auth/login - so users saw React Native's default blank white background\ninstead of the login page, for anywhere from a few hundred ms to several\nseconds on a slower device or release build.\n\nNow shows the same loading indicator for both \"still restoring\" and\n\"restored, no token yet\" states, never an empty render. The actual\nredirect decision stays entirely in _layout.tsx.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
